PHASE C — BUILD (every feature)
C1. Game engine (pure Kotlin, deterministic with seeded RNG, 100% unit-tested)

Formats. 5 overs: 7-a-side, all out at 6 wickets, 2 bowlers may bowl 2 overs and the rest 1, Powerplay = over 1, Slog = over 5. 10 overs: 11-a-side, all out at 10, max 2 overs per bowler, Powerplay = overs 1–2, Slog = overs 9–10. All other overs = Middle. No bowler bowls two overs in a row. If the XI has no WK, the last player in the XI keeps.

Ball pipeline. (1) Bowling roll (red die = row, blue = column) on the right bowling sheet and line → (2) result: 0 dot · X wicket card · + extra (draw Runs card) · Ball → (3) batting roll on the right batting sheet and line → 0/1/2/3/4/6 or X. Row F can return a wicket code directly (no Wicket card drawn). A FOR ALL cell is identical for every line.

Sheet selection: Middle overs → Master Bowling + Master Batting; Powerplay and Slog → Powerplay & Slog Bowling + Batting. Ground (HSG/NSG/LSG) chosen per match (each tournament fixture has its own ground).

Bowling line (Middle): from bowler type × batsman type via the domination table (BW/BWAL/BTAL/BTBW bowler vs BW/BWAL/BTAL-WK/BAT-BTBW batsman → BWD3, BWD2, BWD1, EQ, BTD1, BTD2, BTD3). Batting type mapping: BTBW & BAT → "BT/BTBW"; BTAL & WK → "BTAL/WK"; BWAL → "BWAL"; BW → "BW". BAT and WK do not bowl. Bowling line (PP/Slog): PWP:PC / PWP:SP (pacer/spinner in Powerplay), SLG:PC / SLG:SP, SLG:DB for a death bowler (D mark) in the Slog. Pacers: RF RFM RM LF LFM LM. Spinners: RO RL LO LC. Batting line (Middle): ★ Star past his listed runs → HS/★; BWAL or BW batsman → BWAL/BW; everyone else → HS/★, NS or LS from the matchup grid (bowler style × batsman hand). Batting line (PP/Slog): PWPO openers (O) in Powerplay · PWPR everyone else in Powerplay · SLG F the one Finisher in Slog · SLG R everyone else in Slog · BW for a BW batsman in any of these overs.

Row F rules:

Master Bowling row F — star dominance (set 2): bowling team has MORE stars than batting team → 5★ list; equal stars → middle 4★ list; FEWER → 3★ list. Stars are the match's snapshot stars (see below). Show the label "Bowling team has MORE ★ / SAME ★ / FEWER ★ than the batting team" and the line "★ IND 5★ v PAK 5★ · equal stars: even match".
Master Batting row F — by bowler type. PP&Slog Bowling row F — by bowling-style group. PP&Slog Batting row F — by batsman (★ / BW / BWAL / REST).
Wicket codes: BLD, LBW, HW = out immediately (LBW can be reviewed); CB, ST, C&B = fielder known → draw Skills card only; CT, R/O = Fielding card then Skills card. No Wicket card is drawn when row F names the wicket; log "Row F: X".

Special players:

Star ★: once past his listed runs → HS/★ (Middle) and ★ on row F (PP/Slog).
Finisher (F): only one F batsman acts as Finisher, only in the Slog. Default = first F batsman in the batting order who isn't out; a scorer-chosen Finisher always wins. In the Slog, when a new batsman is about to come in, the Finisher isn't in yet and ≥2 F batsmen are available → ask "Who goes in as the Finisher?"; anyone not picked reads SLG R. Before the Slog he bats by his normal type.
Death bowler (D): SLG:DB line in Slog. Captain (C): holds power cards, one per team. Opener (O): 3 per team.
"At the crease" sheet roles per batsman: Auto · Ignore Star/Opener/Finisher · Treat as Finisher · Force Star ★.

Wicket system. X → draw Wicket card → how out. Kinds: lbw, bowled, caught, caughtBehind, stumped, caughtAndBowled, runOutStriker, runOutNonStriker (non-striker out), hitWicket (only via row-F HW or Custom ball; no card for it). kindFor(card, bowlingStyle): caught-behind cards apply to pacers (LF, RF, LFM, RFM); on other styles the same card reads differently — reconstruct from md §9.2 and the Wicket-cards PDF. Fielder's chance → Fielding card (1–20 = squad number); number not in the Playing XI → "No fielder" (chance goes begging). If the Fielding card names the keeper he counts as keeper; names the bowler → counts as bowler. Skills card: fielder colour (Red best / Green good / Blue average) decides taken vs missed per the 5-row table. Missed chance (catch dropped, stumping missed, run-out miss, no fielder) → draw Runs card. Run-out direct hit: Runs card also gives runs completed before the dismissal.

Extras (app rule, md §10.1). When + comes up, draw a Runs card and use the "Extras (app now)" column: 8 of 16 cards give a plain dot ball (no extra, legal ball); the other 8 give W, W+1, W+2, NB, NB+1, B1, L1, L2 (use the app-now column exactly as printed in md). Wide/no-ball are not legal deliveries. No-ball → next ball is a Free Hit (banner e.g. "NO BALL CALLED! FREE HIT ACTIVATED"). Per md §10 and the Stitch Free Hit & Extras Engine screen: on a Free Hit the app draws a Runs card ("Proceed to Free Hit roll") and that card's Free-hit column resolves the ball directly — the "Free-hit target matrix" shows two values, one for BAT/AL/WK batsmen ("others" column) and one for a BW batsman (own column); runs may be 0–6, no bowling/batting sheet roll. The Stitch screen states that on a free hit Bowled, Caught, LBW and Stumped are NOT OUT and Run out remains a legal dismissal; the md does not say how a run-out arises when a card resolves the ball, so implement: no wicket from the card itself, plus a "Run out on free hit" action available through Custom ball. Log this interpretation in docs/AMBIGUITIES.md. The screen also shows: printed-sheet extras ("16/16 cards yield extras", avg 6.3 extras/innings) vs App engine 2026 (8 of 16 convert to legal dot balls, avg 2.4 extras/innings, −62%); a 16-card blue-deck composition map (dot-conversion cards marked), the drawn card (e.g. "NB+1 — 1 No Ball penalty + 1 run, ball does not count, +2 runs credited"), "Inspect 16 Cards" and "Undo No Ball" buttons, and an "Extras & Balance Guide" (Wide / No Ball / Byes-Leg byes / Dot engine tabs). Show an "Extras help" card. Message: "Extra? Draw a runs card: a wide, no ball, bye or leg bye, or just a dot ball."

Power cards & DRS (md §11). Only captains. Reroll ×2 (one per captain): cancel his own roll and roll again — both dice, or red only, or blue only (Half Reroll, kept die locked); a BW/BWAL captain's Reroll only on the bowling sheet, everyone else's on the batting sheet. Wonderful Shot ×2: BAT/BTBW/BTAL/WK captain while he is on strike, cancels batting roll and rolls the card grid. Great Delivery ×2: BW/BWAL captain while he is bowling, cancels bowling roll and rolls the grid (B → batting roll, + → extra). Played straight after the roll, before anything else; a team never rerolls the other team's roll; allowed on the last ball of an over and after an undo; none in a Super Over. DRS: batting captain given out LBW or caught-behind (also a row-F LBW) may spend his Reroll; roll one die: 5–6 = not out (dot ball). New matches don't give the toss winner an extra Reroll.

Stars. Printed stars: 5★ IND PAK SL AUS; 4★ BAN ENG SA NZ; 3★ AFG WI. Form stars (per format, 5-over and 10-over separate): teams with ≥2 completed matches in that format are ranked by win % (tie = half win), tie-breaks NRR → printed stars → team code; rank 1–4 = 5★, 5–8 = 4★, 9+ = 3★; <2 matches keep printed stars; NRR counts an all-out innings as the full overs quota; Super Overs not counted. At match start both teams' stars are snapshotted into the match and never change mid-match. Show form stars in match setup and a Form-stars table on the Teams page (printed, current, rank, matches, wins, win %, NRR, ▲▼ movement).

Innings / match. Over limits, strike rotation, innings break banner ("Start 2nd innings"), target, CRR, RRR, "Need X off Y", result (win by runs/wickets, tie), 🏆 win banner → "Back to tournament" / "New match". Super Over: each side nominates 3 batsmen + 1 bowler, one over, Slog sheets, 2 wickets end it, no power cards, same sheet set/ground; tied again → another Super Over with players from the last one sitting out; knockout needs a winner (as many as it takes); league/friendly may "Leave it as a tie"; app says who bats first; each Super Over shown separately in Scorecard/Summary/Ball-by-ball.

Decks. Physical-deck behaviour: draw without replacement from the finite deck and reshuffle when exhausted (setting: infinite/with-replacement mode). No card shows a "No. N" number — the UI must not reveal card order/number (fielding position numbers are card content and stay).

Commentary. Per-ball commentary generator in English and Hindi (toggle). Keep all strings in resources.

